⚡️⚡️🇺🇸 The Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI)’s National Crime Information Center was hacked and so far has not been recovered. The National Crime Information Center is more of a division, for those unaware of the structure; however as of concurrent this heavily affects the “National Instant Criminal Background Check System”, commonly referred to as ‘NICS’, which handles the approval/denial/holding for NATIONWIDE firearm purchases in the United States (as all purchases regarding firearms in the US both in-person and online from retail, commercial & wholesale require a Form-4473 which is a NICS background check).

Based off current localized information, it is currently a ‘hit or miss’ when it comes to filing a 4473 to purchase a firearm, with some of them being rejected or failing to send, and some going through, but at large; the system is still down with no stated timeline for recovery.

